1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,046
“Oh no, the water pump died again. The tub is empty.”

2
00:00:06,046 --> 00:00:09,682
When the water pump stops, the whole house waits.

3
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:14,923
Or the motorbike won't start, and the bengkel down the road is closed.

4
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:17,371
So I built Tukang Copilot.

5
00:00:17,371 --> 00:00:22,999
Take a photo, say what's wrong, and it finds the part and walks you through the fix.

6
00:00:23,367 --> 00:00:31,607
From here on, every phone screen is real output from Meta's models, recorded on a live run on November sixth.

7
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:37,812
Pick a photo and say the problem, in Bahasa, Javanese or English.

8
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:41,955
The one-tap demo replays that run on this same photo.

9
00:00:41,955 --> 00:00:45,678
Results show up as each model finishes.

10
00:00:46,033 --> 00:00:52,660
Then the likely cause, how sure it is, and the parts cost next to the bengkel price.

11
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:59,057
SAM 3.1 outlines the real parts on your own photo and numbers them.

12
00:00:59,433 --> 00:01:01,856
A short safety list comes first.

13
00:01:01,856 --> 00:01:05,511
The steps stay locked until every box is ticked.

14
00:01:05,867 --> 00:01:08,160
Then it goes one step at a time.

15
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:16,064
After a step, I send a photo and Muse Spark checks it.

16
00:01:16,064 --> 00:01:18,768
Too dark, so it asks for another.

17
00:01:19,133 --> 00:01:22,512
A clear photo of the plug cap back on passes.

18
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:24,285
Still broken?

19
00:01:24,285 --> 00:01:27,632
It plans again around the next likely cause.

20
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,419
A job for a pro?

21
00:01:29,419 --> 00:01:34,552
One tap hands it to a bengkel, with a WhatsApp summary and a PDF.

22
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:39,396
When a photo can't show a step, Muse Image draws a diagram.

23
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:42,184
It also knows when to say no.

24
00:01:42,767 --> 00:01:50,349
A rice cooker that won't heat means 220-volt parts inside, so it stops and sends you to a service centre.

25
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:53,729
“My bike tyre is flat, there's a nail stuck in it.”

26
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:56,216
It answers in Javanese too.

27
00:01:58,967 --> 00:02:08,452
On the live API, with my earlier sample photos, a repair took a median of 83 seconds and about 4 US cents.

28
00:02:08,452 --> 00:02:16,330
It stopped all 33 dangerous test cases, with no false stops on 17 everyday jobs.

29
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:20,168
Tukang Copilot is open source.

30
00:02:20,168 --> 00:02:22,959
The code is on GitHub, at the link below.
